    test(zimm-text-input): add the conventional beforeEach/afterEach hooks

    .claude/rules/testing.md states the lifecycle hooks without qualification.
    This file's resolvers are pure and it mocks nothing, so the hooks reset no
    observable state — added for consistency with the rule as written rather
    than for isolation, and noted as such at the declaration so the next reader
    doesn't hunt for the shared state they are protecting.

    `base` becomes a `let` reinitialised per test. Typed with the exported
    ZimmTextInputStyleProps rather than an inline literal so the default state
    tracks the resolvers' own signature.

